/E (Exploit \(pre-fix\): A request body containing the _$$ND_FUNC$$_ marker followed by a JavaScript function expression ending in \(\) is sent to /order. During the parsing step,  before any authentication, authorization, or business logic runs, the Lambda's deserializer reconstructs the marker as a function and immediately invokes it. The injected code uses Node's fs module to write /tmp/pwned.txt, read it back, and emit console.error\("FILE READ SUCCESS: ..."\). )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
