/P 439 0 R
/T (The Lambda must verify the JWT signature on every request, not just decode the payload. Specifically, it must \(a\) fetch the JSON Web Key Set \(JWKS\) published by the Cognito User Pool, \(b\) use the appropriate public key to verify the signature cryptographically, and \(c\) reject the request with a 401 if verification fails. Only after successful verification should the username field be trusted. The node-jose library, already imported in order-manager.js, supports this workflow through jose.JWK.asKeyStore\(\) and jose.JWS.createVerify\(\).)
/E (The Lambda must verify the JWT signature on every request, not just decode the payload. Specifically, it must \(a\) fetch the JSON Web Key Set \(JWKS\) published by the Cognito User Pool, \(b\) use the appropriate public key to verify the signature cryptographically, and \(c\) reject the request with a 401 if verification fails. Only after successful verification should the username field be trusted. The node-jose library, already imported in order-manager.js, supports this workflow through jose.JWK.asKeyStore\(\) and jose.JWS.createVerify\(\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
