908 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 455 0 R
/E (The vulnerability is Insecure Cloud Configuration affecting the DVSA feedback S3 bucket. The bucket dvsa-feedback-bucket-448842988219-us-east-1 had an overly permissive bucket policy with Principal: "*" allowing any unauthenticated user on the internet to upload, read, and delete files without any credentials. The security impact is that any anonymous attacker can upload malicious files directly into the bucket, potentially poisoning backend processing or triggering downstream Lambda functions.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
909 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 455 0 R
/E (The S3 bucket had an explicit bucket policy granting Principal: "*" \(everyone\) the actions s3:PutObject, s3:PutObjectAcl, s3:GetObject, and s3:DeleteObject. This means AWS explicitly allows anonymous unauthenticated requests to interact with the bucket. No credentials are required whatsoever.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
