1531 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 508 0 R
/E (When a user submits a request to /order, API Gateway forwards the HTTP body to DVSA-ORDER-MANAGER. The Lambda is expected to parse that body as inert JSON data, extracting fields like action, cart-id, and order-id for routing, and then dispatch the request based on those values. Parsing untrusted input must be a pure data operation: the parser converts text into a data structure and nothing more. No code from the request body should ever be evaluated or executed by the parser itself.)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 508 0 R
/E (Security rules:)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1533 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3438 0 R
/E (R1 \(Safe Parsing\): Untrusted input on the request path must be handled only by parsers that produce inert data structures \(e.g., JSON.parse\(\)\); deserializers that can reconstruct executable functions must never be exposed to attacker-controlled input.)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3439 0 R
/E (R2 \(Dependency Hygiene\): Third-party libraries with known code-execution advisories \(e.g., CVE-2017-5941 for node-serialize\) must not be present on the request path of a public-facing function.)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3440 0 R
/E (R3 \(Minimal Trust Surface\): Every require\(\) is an implicit trust decision; libraries should be imported only when their functionality is actually needed and their security posture has been reviewed.)
/Pg 92 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
