1546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 509 0 R
/E (The exploit violates R1 and R2 simultaneously. R1 is violated because the request path used node-serialize.unserialize\(\), a deserializer that, by design, can reconstruct and invoke functions from input strings, instead of a safe parser. R2 is violated because node-serialize carries a documented code-execution advisory \(CVE-2017-5941\) and should never have been on a public request path. R3 is violated as a contributing factor: the library was imported even though its function-deserialization feature was never required by any legitimate DVSA workflow, JSON.parse\(\) would have sufficed.)
/Pg 93 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
