1579 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1747 0 R
/E (The application imported and used node-serialize.unserialize\(\), a deserializer with a documented function-execution feature \(CVE-2017-5941\), to parse attacker-controlled request bodies. This exposes a remote code execution primitive on a public endpoint, where a safe parser would have rejected the same input.)
/Pg 95 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1748 0 R
/E (Accidental misconfiguration / supply-chain hygiene failure)
/Pg 95 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1749 0 R
/E (Removed require\('node-serialize'\) from DVSA-ORDER-MANAGER/order-manager.js; replaced serialize.unserialize\(event.body\) with JSON.parse\(event.body\) and used event.headers directly \(no deserialization\). Deployed via AWS Console.)
/Pg 95 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
1582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1750 0 R
/E (Replaying the _$$ND_FUNC$$_ payload no longer produces a FILE READ SUCCESS log entry \(CloudWatch search returns "No events found"\); source inspection confirms unserialize\(\) is absent from the request path; a legitimate order placed through the DVSA UI completes end-to-end.)
/Pg 95 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
