1586 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (Vulnerable dependencies are one of the hardest classes of bugs to catch during code review because the vulnerable code is not in the project, it is installed into it. Every require\(\) call is an implicit trust decision, and in serverless projects where functions are small and dependencies are many, it is easy for a single bad package to end up on a critical path. Two lessons:)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1587 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3441 0 R
/E (Dependency hygiene is a security control. Tools like npm audit, lockfile reviews, and CVE monitoring should be part of every deployment pipeline, not an afterthought.)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3442 0 R
/E (Prefer the standard library when possible. JSON.parse\(\) did everything DVSA actually needed; the vulnerable library was providing a feature no legitimate client ever used. Minimizing dependency surface minimizes attack surface.)
/Pg 96 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
