/Title (This is identical to the response User C sees when legitimately requesting their own orders \(verified by the earlier Network-tab capture while logged in as User C\). The server returned User C's $28 Super Mario order and its access token to a request authenticated only by a forged payload. No password was ever used, and the signature was copied verbatim from User B's token, making it invalid for the modified payload.)
