/Title (In serverless architectures, Lambda functions can execute in parallel, and without strict server-side sequencing, an attacker can exploit the time delay between a check \(status verification\) and an action \(updating an order\).)
/Dest [86 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 8841 0 R
/Prev 8845 0 R
/Next 8857 0 R
>>
endobj
8852 0 obj
<<
/Title (In addition, a security-critical threshold \(like > 110\) should never leave room for an "in-between" state \(like 100\) to be treated as valid for updates. The fix demonstrates that moving to >= 100 immediately closes the vulnerability window.)
